        Instead of simulating removals, we look for how the winner changes as N increases.
      </p>

      <h3>2) Key observation: powers of two dominate</h3>
      <p>
        Let p be the largest power of 2 such that p ≤ N, and write N = p + m.
        For this specific across-circle variant, the winner position can be expressed directly in terms of m.
